Title......: HD-Installer for Sim City
Type.......: Hard drive patch (WHDLoad)
Author.....: Galahad of Fairlight, Wepl

This patch applies to "Sim City", ©1989,1991 Maxis/Infogrames

Versions supported (SPS = IPF number of the Software Preservation Society):
  512K  SPS 888, 1870, 2192
  1.0   SPS 1992 (HLS encrypted)
  1.2   SPS 1953, 2193
  CDTV

There are two Slaves:
  SimCity.Slave      floppy versions 512K, 1.0, 1.2 (detected automatically)
                     requires WHDLoad 17+
  SimCityCDTV.Slave  CDTV version, requires WHDLoad 21+

With the tooltype Custom1=1 SimCity.Slave starts the program PrintCity
instead of the game, which prints saved cities. PrintCity exists only on
the 512K disks, version 1.2 has this function built into the game.

SimCity.Slave uses 512 KB Chip + 768 KB Fast memory, SimCityCDTV.Slave
uses 960 KB Chip + 304 KB Fast memory.
Additionally around 1.5 MB (floppy) or 3 MB (CDTV) other memory are
required for preload.
Version 1.0 may run too fast on faster machines, in this case use the
tooltype NoCache or ExpChip.

CD audio (CDTV version):
The CD audio tracks can be played via WHDLoad. This requires audio
hardware supported by WHDLoad. The CD audio tracks 2-19 must be compressed
(e.g. MP3) and copied manually as Track02.mp3 .. Track19.mp3 into the
directory "data-da" created by the installer. Then enable the tooltype
"Audio=data-da" in the icon (remove the leading ';').

The CDTV memory card is not supported. Cities can be saved via the disk
option instead, they are stored as C1.CTY .. C6.CTY in the data directory.

FEATURES:
- Full load from Hard drive (REAL Files)
- Lame-o-Protect removed (Doc Check)
- Save games to Hard drive
- Quit option is 'F10'

Thanks to Exotica for the icons

NOTES:

Started this install a long time ago, and promptly lost the lot in a 
hard drive crash!

In a way, thats a bit of a bonus, because KickDOS has been replaced by
KickEMU and this install now uses files instead of diskimages that it
did when I first did the install, so its better all round.

Version 1.0 NTSC will be released as and when the KickEMU fault can be fixed.  
The copy protection for this version is the rather lame-tastic HLS Ben
Herndon system of Encryption, track check and decryption (2 passes no less!).

This was removed quickly, but there it appears the Maxis method of detecting
NTSC is rather crude, and it only has problems within the WHDLoad environment
and nowhere else, so this leads me to believe its a KickEMU fault.

I can't quite understand why Maxis would choose to use this particularly
stupid protection method for their game.  They put a readme text on the disk
telling you how to install to hard drive, but this copy protection means that
you still need the original disk to be able to continue past the protection
check!! I guess thats why they only used it the once, no other versions
of Sim City carry this useless 'protection'.

The CDTV version of this game expects 1Meg of Chip ram, so it will not work
on any Amigas with less.  This game was never intended to be run on anything
other than a CDTV, so this is to be expected.

Special Regards go out to: Wepl for constantly striving to improve WHDLoad,
Stingray, Magic Mushroom, WayneK, Jope, DLFRSilver, Musashi, KillerGorilla,
and most people from EAB, and everyone from my 'illustrious' past who 
are never forgotten! :)

Regards, Galahad

Version 2.0 (2026-11-08) done by Wepl:
- one Slave for all floppy versions
- versions are detected via checksum, random generator is now initialized
  like on the original (was skipped together with the manual check)
- CDTV: language is taken from the system (lowlevel.library like)
- Custom1 starts PrintCity (512K version)
- version 1.0 supported, the HLS protection is removed without the need of
  the original disk
- ZoneEvolutionChart is copied into the install directory
- CDTV: CD audio tracks are played via WHDLoad (requires WHDLoad 21)
- CDTV: access fault on loading from the memory card fixed, the memory card
  is reported as missing, the disk option must be used instead
- CDTV: memory changed to 960 KB Chip + 304 KB Fast
- cache problem on starting the simulation (512K) or the maps and graphs
  windows (1.x) with Fast memory fixed
- 1.0/1.2: access faults and overwritten exception vectors on drawing into
  the message line and the graphs window before they are opened fixed
- new install script
- source available: https://github.com/wepl/winstalls

         Bug report form, full WHDLoad package and other installs:
                          http://www.whdload.de
